(6402767, 947756, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is a beauty. I missed it before. It makes me think of a "companion piece" I shot a while ago :-)<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=922969" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_922969.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_922969.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_922969.jpg"/></a> <br/></td>', 'This is a beauty. I missed it before. It makes me think of a "companion piece" I shot a while ago :-)  ', '2011-05-03 11:31:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403011, 947245, 124217, '<td valign="top">I totally agree with colorcarnival, if this shot has a a flower or a bird would be #1. This is a very difficult to shot to take thats why it would deserve higher rating, no doubt. Again congrats for the work and thank you for sharing this great work!</td>', 'I totally agree with colorcarnival, if this shot has a a flower or a bird would be #1. This is a very difficult to shot to take thats why it would deserve higher rating, no doubt. Again congrats for the work and thank you for sharing this great work!', '2011-05-03 15:51:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403163, 947245, 55822, '<td valign="top">As has been said before, this should have done better. It was actually one of my highest votes for this challenge. I have a feeling many dont understand how hard this was to capture with the ball being that sharp. Great job.</td>', 'As has been said before, this should have done better. It was actually one of my highest votes for this challenge. I have a feeling many dont understand how hard this was to capture with the ball being that sharp. Great job.', '2011-05-03 20:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403254, 947902, 83754, '<td valign="top">Thank you for the comments.  Considering I''m usually in the 4s, I''m happy with the almost 6.  As this was a bokeh challenge and I realize that the noticible water reflections from the pond behind the stork are not smooth and could be a distraction to those looking for one.  The stork and I did sit and watch each other for some time to get a pose and lighting I liked.</td>', 'Thank you for the comments.  Considering I''m usually in the 4s, I''m happy with the almost 6.  As this was a bokeh challenge and I realize that the noticible water reflections from the pond behind the stork are not smooth and could be a distraction to those looking for one.  The stork and I did sit and watch each other for some time to get a pose and lighting I liked.', '2011-05-03 21:32:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403562, 947245, 90495, '<td valign="top">Great superb capture. I would have thought it had taken way more than 30 shots.</td>', 'Great superb capture. I would have thought it had taken way more than 30 shots.', '2011-05-04 01:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403591, 947045, 41337, '<td valign="top">This is very symbolic of your work. If I could describe it in one word it would be <i>uplifting</i>.</td>', 'This is very symbolic of your work. If I could describe it in one word it would be uplifting.', '2011-05-04 02:02:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403691, 947766, 31727, '<td valign="top">Very nice and hard to do.</td>', 'Very nice and hard to do.', '2011-05-04 03:58:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403710, 947208, 43594, '<td valign="top">Amazing one, Dan. Congrats!</td>', 'Amazing one, Dan. Congrats!', '2011-05-04 04:33:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403812, 947245, 41676, '<td valign="top">I love it. This is the highest rated picture that does not depend on animals or immovable objects! It may not have gotten the marks you wanted but I would think it would be a very sellable picture. Nice Job!</td>', 'I love it. This is the highest rated picture that does not depend on animals or immovable objects! It may not have gotten the marks you wanted but I would think it would be a very sellable picture. Nice Job!', '2011-05-04 08:57:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403870, 947245, 100831, '<td valign="top">Should have placed higher. I marvel at the skill involved.</td>', 'Should have placed higher. I marvel at the skill involved.', '2011-05-04 09:44:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(6403884, 947245, 72670, '<td valign="top">It scored lower than expected because it didn''t fall into the "flower or bug" category. Voters very rarely think outside the box. I didn''t vote in this challenge.<br/> <br/>Great execution!<br/> <br/>The only thing i would prefer is not so much blur on the actors. :)<br/> <br/>Edit iPad error.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-05-04 08:54:31.</i></td>', 'It scored lower than expected because it didn''t fall into the "flower or bug" category. Voters very rarely think outside the box. I didn''t vote in this challenge. Great execution! The only thing i would prefer is not so much blur on the actors. :) Edit iPad error.', '2011-05-04 09:51:27.000000', '2011-05-04 09:54:31.000000', 0),
(6404001, 947245, 48954, '<td valign="top">underrated!</td>', 'underrated!', '2011-05-04 11:20:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404039, 947245, 101117, '<td valign="top">It didn''t score well because it''s too real, simple as that.<br/> <br/>It''s not a setup, perfectly pretty, macro / portrait / photoshop creation, it''s a real journalist (very well captured) sporting shot.<br/> <br/>This shot belongs somewhere else where people will "get it", not at DPC.</td>', 'It didn''t score well because it''s too real, simple as that. It''s not a setup, perfectly pretty, macro / portrait / photoshop creation, it''s a real journalist (very well captured) sporting shot. This shot belongs somewhere else where people will "get it", not at DPC.', '2011-05-04 11:50:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404045, 947779, 75585, '<td valign="top">William - you just continue to ''slam-dunk'' challenges.  Your talent is amazing!  The only thing I would change is the catchlight in the drop makes me think it was done in studio and I wish it wasn''t there altering that gorgeous reflection in the droplet.  But nonetheless I still love it!  Reminds me of our native water droplet photographer in Portland Steve Terrill.</td>', 'William - you just continue to ''slam-dunk'' challenges.  Your talent is amazing!  The only thing I would change is the catchlight in the drop makes me think it was done in studio and I wish it wasn''t there altering that gorgeous reflection in the droplet.  But nonetheless I still love it!  Reminds me of our native water droplet photographer in Portland Steve Terrill.', '2011-05-04 12:05:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404237, 947176, 119747, '<td valign="top">A high 4?! This is a fantastic shot, did not expect to see the spider in the bottom corner as I scrolled down! Brilliant colours</td>', 'A high 4?! This is a fantastic shot, did not expect to see the spider in the bottom corner as I scrolled down! Brilliant colours', '2011-05-04 14:54:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404284, 947943, 66384, '<td valign="top">Timmy, this is marvelous. I don''t know what it is or how you managed to see this, but it is the ultimate bokeh. And I like your artistic processing!</td>', 'Timmy, this is marvelous. I don''t know what it is or how you managed to see this, but it is the ultimate bokeh. And I like your artistic processing!', '2011-05-04 15:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404292, 947875, 66384, '<td valign="top">I love the back lighting on this, and the beautiful focus. I''m thinking this would have done better in a shallow DOF challenge. Although you have blur in the foreground and background, it doesn''t really say ''bokeh'' to me. Still you have a marvelous photograph. Are you going to hang it in your kitchen?</td>', 'I love the back lighting on this, and the beautiful focus. I''m thinking this would have done better in a shallow DOF challenge. Although you have blur in the foreground and background, it doesn''t really say ''bokeh'' to me. Still you have a marvelous photograph. Are you going to hang it in your kitchen?', '2011-05-04 15:44:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404313, 947245, 97166, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote, but here''s my take:<br/> <br/>In a bokeh challenge, the key is to get the bokeh to be the defining feature of the shot.  You should be able to look at the photo and say, "The background elements contribute to the overall feeling of the photo".  Is that what can be said about this shot? Well, not really.<br/> <br/>What defines this shot IS the frozen ball. Period. It''s the whole reason the shot exists, and the whole reason for looking at the photo.  It''s "Wow, he got a ball frozen in time during a pitch! cool!"  However, we don''t even care one iota about background elements.  They are secondary and provide no meaning to the photo.<br/> <br/>In a bokeh challenge, you need the BOKEH to be what''s looked at and talked about. Instead, you have the ball being that primary aspect, and the ball isn''t bokeh. <br/> <br/>Quite frankly, a 6.2+ is far more than this shot probably SHOULD have got, but you scored higher than I would have thought it would have placed because you did manage to wow people with the frozen action and got them to look past the fact that bokeh plays no part.  So instead of looking negatively that the score might have been higher, look positively that it''s actually as high as it is.</td>', 'I didn''t vote, but here''s my take: In a bokeh challenge, the key is to get the bokeh to be the defining feature of the shot.  You should be able to look at the photo and say, "The background elements contribute to the overall feeling of the photo".  Is that what can be said about this shot? Well, not really. What defines this shot IS the frozen ball. Period. It''s the whole reason the shot exists, and the whole reason for looking at the photo.  It''s "Wow, he got a ball frozen in time during a pitch! cool!"  However, we don''t even care one iota about background elements.  They are secondary and provide no meaning to the photo. In a bokeh challenge, you need the BOKEH to be what''s looked at and talked about. Instead, you have the ball being that primary aspect, and the ball isn''t bokeh.  Quite frankly, a 6.2+ is far more than this shot probably SHOULD have got, but you scored higher than I would have thought it would have placed because you did manage to wow people with the frozen action and got them to look past the fact that bokeh plays no part.  So instead of looking negatively that the score might have been higher, look positively that it''s actually as high as it is.', '2011-05-04 16:30:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404317, 947245, 45524, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K10DGuy:</b></div><hr/><i> I didn''t vote, but here''s my take:<br/> <br/>In a bokeh challenge, the key is to get the bokeh to be the defining feature of the shot.  You should be able to look at the photo and say, "The background elements contribute to the overall feeling of the photo".  Is that what can be said about this shot? Well, not really.<br/> <br/>What defines this shot IS the frozen ball. Period. It''s the whole reason the shot exists, and the whole reason for looking at the photo.  It''s "Wow, he got a ball frozen in time during a pitch! cool!"  However, we don''t even care one iota about background elements.  They are secondary and provide no meaning to the photo.<br/> <br/>In a bokeh challenge, you need the BOKEH to be what''s looked at and talked about. Instead, you have the ball being that primary aspect, and the ball isn''t bokeh. <br/> <br/>Quite frankly, a 6.2+ is far more than this shot probably SHOULD have got, but you scored higher than I would have thought it would have placed because you did manage to wow people with the frozen action and got them to look past the fact that bokeh plays no part.  So instead of looking negatively that the score might have been higher, look positively that it''s actually as high as it is. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Really? You think the person who threw that ball and the person that caught that ball has nothing to with telling the story of the ball? To me the people in this photo tell the story.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-05-04 16:40:22.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by K10DGuy: I didn''t vote, but here''s my take: In a bokeh challenge, the key is to get the bokeh to be the defining feature of the shot.  You should be able to look at the photo and say, "The background elements contribute to the overall feeling of the photo".  Is that what can be said about this shot? Well, not really. What defines this shot IS the frozen ball. Period. It''s the whole reason the shot exists, and the whole reason for looking at the photo.  It''s "Wow, he got a ball frozen in time during a pitch! cool!"  However, we don''t even care one iota about background elements.  They are secondary and provide no meaning to the photo. In a bokeh challenge, you need the BOKEH to be what''s looked at and talked about. Instead, you have the ball being that primary aspect, and the ball isn''t bokeh.  Quite frankly, a 6.2+ is far more than this shot probably SHOULD have got, but you scored higher than I would have thought it would have placed because you did manage to wow people with the frozen action and got them to look past the fact that bokeh plays no part.  So instead of looking negatively that the score might have been higher, look positively that it''s actually as high as it is.   Really? You think the person who threw that ball and the person that caught that ball has nothing to with telling the story of the ball? To me the people in this photo tell the story.', '2011-05-04 16:37:53.000000', '2011-05-04 17:40:22.000000', 0),
(6404327, 947245, 123348, '<td valign="top">Great shot indeed! Wow....</td>', 'Great shot indeed! Wow....', '2011-05-04 16:48:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404474, 947208, 51269, '<td valign="top">You are amazing &amp; so is your image- I''m happy to see the equipment you use :-)</td>', 'You are amazing & so is your image- I''m happy to see the equipment you use :-)', '2011-05-04 20:29:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404577, 947245, 106233, '<td valign="top">Wow!<br/>Totally underrated image.<br/>I did not vote on this challenge, but your picture would be my choice for the blue ribbon. I agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=41337" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">yanko</a> about the tight crop, but even so the picture is outstanding.<br/>Congratulations!!</td>', 'Wow!Totally underrated image.I did not vote on this challenge, but your picture would be my choice for the blue ribbon. I agree with  yanko about the tight crop, but even so the picture is outstanding.Congratulations!!', '2011-05-04 22:26:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6404836, 947766, 65311, '<td valign="top">Perfect!<br/></td>', 'Perfect!', '2011-05-05 07:48:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6405362, 947176, 93565, '<td valign="top">Man, this is a great shot! I hadn''t seen it before, but you''ve captured it perfectly. The bokeh is nice, but the point of view is what sells this image, with the radiating web and the spider lurking at the center. Very nice.</td>', 'Man, this is a great shot! I hadn''t seen it before, but you''ve captured it perfectly. The bokeh is nice, but the point of view is what sells this image, with the radiating web and the spider lurking at the center. Very nice.', '2011-05-05 23:09:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6405434, 947331, 132057, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful!</td>', 'Very beautiful!', '2011-05-06 01:23:48.000000', NULL, 0),
